  "attrs": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "datasheet - the material, the finish, the standards (c(UL)us, RoHS, EIA 310.E) and the four #12-24 screws supplied are the specification sheet's; \"Color: Black\" is the product page's."
  },
  "cable-capacity": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "datasheet - Leviton's application note \"Maximum Cable Fill Ratios in Cable Managers\" (NS-AN-23-006-05-30-23, 5/30/2023), page 11: \"Ring size: 4.0 sq.in. (49253-LPM)\", and for the 6AS10 patch cord (0.240 in) 44 cords at 50 percent fill, 26 at 30 percent, 22 at 25 percent. It states 30 percent as the \"recommended practical maximum\" for patch cords in front managers, and gives its worked example of 24 cords through the end ring at 27.1 percent. The count is a ring's: each of the five has the same opening, and the note counts the cords through the busiest. It names the cord by Leviton part number and not by category, so no `cable-capacity-media` is stated."
  },
  "chassis": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - 444.5 x 43.7 x 114.3. The plate is flat over the whole 19.00 in [482.6mm] and its top and bottom edges fold back from 0.75 in [19.05mm] inside each end to 17.5 in [463.55mm], so the flat ends outside the folds are the ears, which this library does not draw (they carry two slots each, 10.4 x 7.1 mm, centred 6.0 mm from the top and bottom edge), and the body is the 444.5. The specification sheet's overall depth is 4.50 in [114.3mm]: the rings 4.00 in [101.6mm] from the face of the plate, the sheet 1.5 and the fold 11.2 behind it."
  },
  "color": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - \"Color: Black\" and \"black powder-coat finish\". The drawing is line work and the product images were not used, so the shade is this library's render of black."
  },
  "cover": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - the 49253-1CV cover is a separate part sold separately (specification sheet: \"Covers are available (sold separately)\"), so the manager is drawn without it; the `with-cover` configuration fits it. The instruction sheet, step 3, says to align the cover's sides to the outside split rings and slide it down until fully seated. Nothing says the cover is hinged."
  },
  "ears": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - `positions` states where the ears bolt, for the Rack Builder. The ears are the flat ends of the panel, so the ear plane is the panel, and its back face is the one that meets the rail: the top view of the 49253-LPM dimensional drawing dimensions the plate's front face 101.6 mm [4.00 in] behind the ring tips and the sheet 1.5 mm, so `at` is 103.1. Of the 114.3 depth, 11.2 stands behind the rail. This states a placement; no dimension changed."
  },
  "front": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - the front view: the plate between the folds and the five rings on it. Rings centred 26.1 mm from the left end of the 482.6 and 107.6 apart (the first at 21.35 to 30.85, the others 128.95, 236.55, 344.15 and 451.75), symmetric about the middle, 38.1 mm high and centred on the 43.7 plate (2.8 above and below). Leviton's mark, printed on the plate near the right ring, is not drawn: a vendor mark never is."
  },
  "full-depth": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "`full-depth: false` - the rings stand 101.6 mm in front of the panel and its folded edges reach only 11.2 behind it (the side view), so the rear face of its rack unit stays free for another part."
  },
  "guides": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - the five rings are the guides: each a component with a `ring` guide (see its contract), cables passing along the panel through each in turn. The opening is 31.75 x 82.55 mm, 4.06 sq in, and Leviton's application note gives the ring's cross-section as 4.0 sq in."
  },
  "left": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - an elevation, the drawing's side view: the folded edges behind the plate and the ring's profile in front of it. The right is the same, turned round."
  },
  "method": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "FIGURES FROM THE MAKER'S OWN DIMENSIONAL DRAWING. Leviton publishes the 49253-LPM drawing as DXF and DWG on its product page; the DXF is vector CAD in inches with five views (front, top, side, rear, isometric), and its dimensions read 19.00 in, 1.72 in, 4.0 in, 3.5 in and 4.5 in. Every figure here is read from its line work at 25.4 mm to the inch and agrees with those dimensions and with the specification sheet's page 2 (482.6, 43.7, 101.6 and 114.3 mm). Where the specification sheet and the drawing disagree, the drawing is taken: see `rings`."
  },
  "rear": {
